 "literal": "Dense moist hair bright forehead young woman / fragrant cool she of the nature of water rare she has tormented indeed / \"she is of this nature\" saying her to describe limit I do not know / few are very soft words / mattress soft she I embracing at the time",
 "translation": "The young woman with dense, moist hair and a bright forehead has the nature of fragrant, cool water, and she has tormented me like a goddess. I do not know how to describe her, saying, 'She is like this.' Her words are few and very soft. And when I embrace her, she is softer than a mattress.",
 "modern": "அடர்ந்த ஈரமான கூந்தலையும் ஒளிரும் நெற்றியையும் உடைய இளம்பெண், நறுமணமிக்க குளிர்ந்த நீரின் தன்மையைக் கொண்டவள்; அவள் எனக்கு அணங்கு போன்றவள் ஆயினாள். 'இவள் இப்படிப்பட்டவள்' என்று அவளைப் புகழ்ந்துரைக்கும் எல்லையை நான் அறியேன். அவளுடைய சொற்கள் சிலவே, அவை மிகவும் மென்மையானவை. நான் அவளைத் தழுவும்போது, அவள் மெத்தையை விடவும் மென்மையானவள் ஆவாள்.",
 "explanation": "The speaker is the hero, expressing his deep love and admiration for the heroine. He describes her physical and behavioral qualities, noting that her hair is dense and moist, and her forehead is bright. He compares her nature to fragrant, cool water, which is both refreshing and tormenting to his heart like a celestial deity. He confesses that he cannot find the words to fully describe her beauty and nature. Her speech is sparse and gentle, and when he embraces her, her body feels softer than a soft mattress. This poem belongs to the Kuriñci tiṇai, representing the union of lovers and the intense, intimate feelings of the hero.",
